    "read_html": "<p><strong>Part III: Delegation and Information Problems (1 hour)</strong></p>\n<p>[READ] Principals monitor agents through two methods:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Police Patrols</strong>: Active, continuous monitoring (costly but comprehensive)</li>\n<li><strong>Fire Alarms</strong>: Wait for complaints from affected parties (cheap but incomplete)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Consider Congress overseeing environmental regulation:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Monitoring Type</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Cost</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Coverage</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Information Quality</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Example</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Police Patrol</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Systematic</td>\n<td>Detailed</td>\n<td>Regular EPA audits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fire Alarm</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>Sporadic</td>\n<td>May miss problems</td>\n<td>Wait for citizen complaints</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Example:</strong> Traffic Safety</td>\n<td>High</td>\n<td>Systematic</td>\n<td>Catches most violations</td>\n<td><strong>Speed traps, patrol cars</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Example:</strong> Traffic Safety</td>\n<td>Low</td>\n<td>Hit-or-miss</td>\n<td>Only egregious cases</td>\n<td><strong>Citizen reports of dangerous driving</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>[Quick Guide]:</strong> Police patrols = principal actively looking. Fire alarms = waiting for others to complain. Think about when each is more effective.</p>",
