    "read_html": "<h2>The European Climate Council Budget Allocation</h2>\n<p>The European Climate Council must decide how to allocate climate funding. Three equal-sized voting blocs have different visions for how to spend these funds.</p>\n<h3>Part A: The Two-Dimensional Policy Space</h3>\n<p>The council must decide spending levels on two programs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Dimension A:</strong> Renewable Energy Subsidies (€0-100 billion)</li>\n<li><strong>Dimension B:</strong> Carbon Capture Research (€0-100 billion)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Three equal blocs (3 members each) with ideal points:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Environmental Bloc:</strong> (A=75, B=50) - Heavy renewable focus, moderate carbon capture</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Bloc:</strong> (A=30, B=60) - Low renewables, high carbon capture focus</li>\n<li><strong>Skeptic Bloc:</strong> (A=25, B=25) - Minimal spending on both programs</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Status Quo:</strong> (A=40, B=40) - Last year's allocation</p>\n<p>All blocs have circular indifference curves (Euclidean preferences).</p>",
